  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local Economic Growth Support Project Second Phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed LEGS 2 Project will build on the successes of the First Phase (LEGS 1) while deepening the processes commenced. The LEGS 1 design created the needed interface between Infrastructure for increasing Agricultural Productivity and Marketing as well as provision of Affordable Rural Financing to support the growth of a Wide Range of Micro to Medium Enterprises. LEGS II will therefore consolidate, deepen and scale-up the successes of LEGS I while addressing the gaps and lessons learned.  

The overall Goal of the Project is: &#x201c;To contribute to achievement of Uganda Vision 2040 and Sustainable Development Goals by accelerating equitable economic growth for improved Livelihoods and incomes of communities and households.

The specific Objectives of the project are the following:

A. To increase Agricultural Production and Productivity for Agribusiness Development and Food Security through provision of Water for Production 



B. To increase the % of Small Holder Farmers engaging in Commercialized Agriculture through access to Economic Infrastructure and Strong Business Institutions for Local and Regional Development



C. To increase access to Affordable and Sustainable Rural Microfinance for Value Chain Development</narrative>
  </description>
